# Release contract for the public boringtun-cli artifacts. See
# docs/BORINGTUN_ARTIFACTS.md, "Publishing a release".
#
# This file is data, not shell: scripts/boringtun-release.sh parses it with the
# same strict KEY=VALUE grammar as pin.env and never sources it. It names one
# exact release of the pin in pin.env and refuses any disagreement with it: the
# release workflow publishes only archives whose bytes, contents and embedded
# binaries match every hash below, from a successful, attested run of the
# BoringTun Artifacts workflow.
#
# BORINGTUN_RELEASE_STATE is `candidate` until the maintainers approve this
# exact release; the workflow never publishes a candidate. A candidate can be
# checked end to end with the workflow's dry-run mode.
#
# BORINGTUN_RELEASE_BUILD counts builds of one source commit: it goes up with
# every change of toolchain, build flags, packaging or notices that changes the
# archive bytes. A published tag is never reused or moved, so once a build is
# public, different bytes need a new build number.
#
# Candidate release: build 1 of the source checkpoint e94c04f3f4fd (tree
# 06402779b8138f4e607b2469c1031e3e910122ca, upstream tag
# awg3.1-integration-2026-10-12), as BoringTun Artifacts run 38254815069
# (branch codex/boringtun-e94c04f-candidate, installer workflow commit
# 3ed28dcbf1c633694580a700a150540af7638913) built it natively on x86_64 and
# aarch64; the x86_64 build was also reproduced byte for byte on another
# machine, and aarch64 was not reproduced outside CI. That run's attestations
# name the branch, not main: they are preparation evidence, not publication
# provenance. Publication still needs a BoringTun Artifacts run of main that
# reproduces these bytes, a BoringTun Release dry run of that run, and a
# separate approval change. The installer embeds the published release of the
# previous pin, boringtun-cli-0.7.1-gb94943906b11-b1, until a later, separate
# adoption change; it, boringtun-cli-0.7.1-gae2ab44e9a68-b1 and
# boringtun-cli-0.7.1-g71d88784ad29-b1 are untouched. The build number starts
# again at 1 because it counts builds of one source commit.
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_FORMAT=1
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_STATE=candidate
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_SOURCE_COMMIT=e94c04f3f4fdb8b392f9586db07a269ea0bf7575
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_VERSION=0.7.1
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_ARTIFACT_FORMAT=1
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_BUILD=1
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_TAG=boringtun-cli-0.7.1-ge94c04f3f4fd-b1
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_ASSET_X86_64=boringtun-cli-0.7.1-ge94c04f3f4fd-linux-x86_64-musl.tar.gz
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_ARCHIVE_SHA256_X86_64=6614814d11cbec37cf65c40887822af9866ac5abc05929332968737c39c6af68
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_BINARY_SHA256_X86_64=7c717357554a4d8022154fbdb1c40c92de8174ee064e81878fdf5f610651fb79
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_ASSET_AARCH64=boringtun-cli-0.7.1-ge94c04f3f4fd-linux-aarch64-musl.tar.gz
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_ARCHIVE_SHA256_AARCH64=a2d7c4a0cc702a7dfc146036e6bda6e341701a3609a6842462bfdbebf7490880
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_BINARY_SHA256_AARCH64=cc1cdf215bb3d75f8a7006f8d424d698e9574dadb3e08becd8ace17a3c44cb08
